---
title: GKOS Canonical Architecture — informative · r3 · v0.82 development candidate
---
flowchart TB
    accTitle: GKOS canonical informative architecture orientation
    accDescr: GKOS defines governance responsibilities, GKX is the interoperability seam, implementations are plural, retrieval and governance remain separate when retrieval is used, governed actions preserve L4 through L7 boundaries, receipts are cross-layer, external bindings are informative, and founder deployment examples are not part of the Standard.

    STD["GKOS Governance Standard<br/>normative source · v0.81 published 2026-09-03 · owner-authorized · non-consensus · no qualifying profile"]
    GKX["GKX 2.0 Data Contracts — interoperability seam<br/>exchange governed records, schemas, fixtures and receipts — not implementation internals<br/>current machine namespace: gkx_version · .gkx/ · GKX-* · gkx"]

    subgraph IMPL["Implementations are plural — examples and evidence targets, not profile qualification"]
        direction LR
        ENG["GKOS-Engine<br/>reference implementation example · inspected package 2.1.2 · TypeScript<br/>no runtime dependencies entry · Graphiti export adapter<br/>implementation mechanism only · development head distinct from conformance"]
        SAME["Additional implementation candidate (same-author)<br/>public source, lineage, fixtures and review evidence pending<br/>evidence target: interoperability · no current public result"]
        INDEP["Public independent-implementation slot<br/>publicly reviewable · independently controlled interpretation and operation<br/>evidence target: independence of implementation and interpretation"]
    end

    subgraph RRET["Provisional v0.82 retrieval-to-context pattern — applies when retrieval is used · non-normative · non-qualifying"]
        direction LR
        RET["Relevance retrieval<br/>may rank an ineligible object first"] --> CAND["Exact candidate set<br/>preserve returned identifiers and raw rank"] --> ELIG["Governance eligibility evaluation<br/>separate from retrieval · no raw-rank rewrite"] --> SUFF["Eligible-candidate sufficiency<br/>none eligible → expand, abstain or escalate"] --> CTX["L6 context assembly<br/>captured Selection Set · deterministic Context Manifest"]
    end

    GAB["Governed Action Boundary<br/>L4 deterministic controls · applicable L5 disposition · L6 Context Manifest verification<br/>L7 authority and effect-scope admission · mandatory failures fail closed<br/>applicable outcome bound to Decision, State-Change, Authorized Use or Refusal evidence"]

    RECORDS["Governance records and receipts — cross-layer<br/>durable, integrity-verifiable record roles<br/>implementation-selected storage · no required universal ledger"]

    AUTH["Authorized humans and bounded reviewers<br/>authority derives from valid grants and controlling policy, not actor class<br/>bounded L5 review may use a human or an authorized independent Review Agent under R18<br/>mandatory R18 escalation routes to an authorized human · observers see only authorized views"]

    subgraph BIND["External bindings — exact-versioned · informative · non-activating under R21 · callable ≠ authorized"]
        direction LR
        MCP["MCP binding<br/>tool, resource, task, context and effect-surface mapping"]
        A2A["A2A binding<br/>agent, task, message, artifact and bounded-delegation mapping"]
        ACS["ACS crosswalk / adapter<br/>observation and enforcement integration · not a dependency"]
    end

    subgraph ACTORS["Governed actor classes — capability does not create authority"]
        direction LR
        READ["Read-only actors<br/>authorized read and projection scope"]
        PROPOSE["Proposal-producing actors<br/>proposals enter applicable controls and review"]
        EFFECT["Governed writers / effect executors<br/>separately authorized · bounded state-change or effect scope"]
    end

    ACTORCONTRACT["Specialized Agent Contract or equivalent governed actor contract<br/>identity · owner · purpose · capabilities · prohibitions · scope · delegation · expiry · evaluation"]

    subgraph DEPLOY["Founder implementation examples — informative overlay, NOT part of the Standard"]
        direction LR
        HYP["Hypatia<br/>model-routing implementation example"]
        OBS["GKOS-Observatory<br/>public demonstration / sandbox example"]
        KO["Kosmos-Oden<br/>human-facing observability example · display grants no authority"]
    end

    LEGEND["Legend<br/>solid arrows = represented control / data path<br/>dashed arrows = governed records, receipts, or implementation attachment<br/>dashed grey boxes = informative external bindings · dashed blue box = open public implementation slot<br/>shaded region = founder implementation examples"]

    STD --> GKX
    GKX --> ENG & SAME & INDEP
    ENG -.-> RET
    SAME -.-> RET
    INDEP -.-> RET
    CTX -->|candidate context or proposed operation| GAB

    AUTH -->|valid authority and applicable disposition| GAB
    GAB -.->|receipts, refusals and escalations| AUTH
    GAB -.->|applicable governed records| RECORDS
    EFFECT -.->|committed governed state change → State-Change Receipt| RECORDS
    RECORDS -.->|governance records exchange through GKX| GKX

    READ -->|authorized read or projection request| GAB
    PROPOSE -->|proposal or review request| GAB
    EFFECT -->|state-change or effect request| GAB
    ACTORCONTRACT --> READ & PROPOSE & EFFECT

    GAB -.- MCP
    GAB -.- A2A
    GAB -.- ACS

    HYP -.-> ACTORS
    OBS -.-> ENG
    KO -.-> AUTH
    DEPLOY -.-> LEGEND

